## Connected tools (MCP)

Apps, CRMs, and ERPs connect to Tantra over MCP only with the user's explicit approval. The user says "mk connect <app>" and the `tantra-connect` skill (main thread only) shows an approval card, opens a config-bound approval gate, and prints the `claude mcp add …` command for the user to run. Approved servers are recorded in `memory/mcp_connections.jsonl`; a server or tool not recorded there as connected is not approved, and write tools need their own `mcp_write_connection` approval. Agents never connect, authenticate, or call unapproved connectors, and secrets never go in chat — environment variables or OAuth only.

## Deliverables & provenance

File deliverables go in `deliverables/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>/`. The Tantra Seal hook signs every file written there automatically (C2PA manifest + Ed25519 `<file>.tantra-sig.json` sidecar), declaring AI involvement honestly — never describe a deliverable as human-only. Verify any sealed file with `python ~/Tantra/.claude/lib/provenance.py verify-file <path>`.

